Third-party components
----------------------

OpenFlux source and release artifacts include the following third-party
components, each under its own license. License texts are kept next to each
component and are included in every release artifact that ships it.

littlefs
  Used by: keyboard firmware, firmware unit tests
  License: BSD-3-Clause (third_party/littlefs/LICENSE.md)

Raspberry Pi Pico SDK
  Used by: keyboard firmware (compiled into the .uf2 image)
  License: BSD-3-Clause

TinyUSB
  Used by: keyboard firmware (compiled into the .uf2 image)
  License: MIT

  The license texts for the libraries compiled into the firmware are published
  with each firmware release as openflux-firmware-licenses.txt.

Montserrat font family
  Used by: keyboard display, desktop app
  License: SIL Open Font License 1.1 (assets/bundled_fonts/LICENSE)

Weather Icons
  Used by: keyboard display, desktop app
  License: SIL Open Font License 1.1 (assets/weather_icons/LICENSE)

Lucide icons
  Used by: keyboard display, desktop app
  License: ISC; portions derived from Feather Icons under the MIT License
  (assets/LUCIDE_LICENSE)

FFmpeg
  Used by: keyboard display package (openflux-ffmpeg) and desktop installers
  (media import), shipped as separate executables invoked over pipes.
  License: the keyboard build is LGPL-2.1-or-later. The desktop builds include
  libx264 and are GPL-2.0-or-later. The exact source code, configure flags and
  build scripts for every shipped FFmpeg binary are published with the
  release that contains it.

libusb
  Used by: desktop installers (openfluxd, through the libusb1-sys crate)
  License: LGPL-2.1-or-later. libusb (LGPL-2.1-or-later) is statically linked
  into openfluxd. The complete corresponding source and build instructions
  for openfluxd are in this repository at each host release tag, so it can be
  rebuilt with a modified libusb. The license text is installed with
  openfluxd in licenses/openfluxd-rust-licenses.txt.

Rust crates and npm packages
  The CycloneDX software bills of materials published with each release list
  every Rust crate and npm package compiled into its binaries and its license.
  The license texts of those dependencies are installed with each binary in a
  licenses/ directory.
